 a seed to\nshaping. An unverifiable or unreadable session points to checking in Shape, never\nclaims readiness; other ended sessions are named as ended.\n\n## Tend: garden and detail\n\nInside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\norigin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\n`a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\nall goals show without a toggle. Unknown, missing, older or conflicting records\nnever guess a repo; those goals remain under all. An empty repo view still offers\n`a`. If any active goal lacks attributable repo information, say `N goals have no\nreadable repo record. Press a for all goals.`, not that this repo has no goals.\nExplicit no-repo records are known non-matches; older records without repo\n\n[972 more lines in file. Use offset=36 to continue.]\n==> text 3/4 <==\n            return;\n        }\n        let keep = self.current().map(|s| s.path.clone());\n        self.show_all = !self.show_all;\n        self.filter_sessions();\n        self.prepare_graph();\n        self.selected = keep\n            .and_then(|path| self.sessions.iter().position(|s| s.path == path))\n            .unwrap_or(0);\n        self.last_press = None;\n        self.graph.release();\n        self.notice.clear();\n    }\n\n    /// Whether the saved-goal garden is showing, rather than detail or a discovery state.\n    pub(super) fn garden_showing(&self) -> bool {\n        !self.detail\n            && !self.pending\n            && self.want.is_none()\n            && self.error.is_none()\n            && !self.sessions.is_empty()\n    }\n    pub(super) fn release_pointer(&mut self) {\n        self.graph.release();\n    }\n    /// Forward pointer mechanics to graf; only Tend can select, link or open a saved goal.\n    pub(super) fn pointer(\n        &mut self,\n        event: crossterm::event::MouseEvent,\n        body: Rect,\n\n[426 more lines in file. Use offset=295 to continue.]\n==> text 4/4 <==\n{\"output\":\"diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md\\nindex f04f156..606551b 100644\\n--- a/AGENTS.md\\n+++ b/AGENTS.md\\n@@ -164,3 +164,9 @@ stubs prove mechanics, not real-dump goal quality.\\n ## Response style\\n \\n Only respond to the user using ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English and the Bottom Line Up Front (BLUF) approach. Use SBAR for handovers and status updates. These do not apply to code or when the user asks otherwise\\n+\\n+<!-- tink:rules begin skillset=build-skillset digest=1f3d3f07b904318d51e96afd8174591e82cabe8ec2da6668bf084aa4d683d4c1 -->\\n+Discipline rules for this phase (compiled by tink; do not edit by hand):\\n+- principle-build-the-lever: Apply to any non-trivial work, not just bulk work: edits, migrations, analyses, checks. Build the tool that does it or proves it (codemod, script, generator, or a skill your subagents follow) instead of working by hand. The tool is the artifact a reviewer can rerun. (read: tink mount principle-build-the-lever --json --payload)\\n+- unslop: Cut AI tells from any writing. Must always apply. (read: tink mount unslop --json --payload)\\n+<!-- tink:rules end -->\\nfull-check totals 1119 passed 1 failed 20 test groups\\nrust totals 1119 passed 1 failed 20 test groups\\npython 86 files 62 passed 24 failed\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"exit_code\":0,\"wall_time_seconds\":0.5}"}],"details":{"calls":[{"id":"call_0435f3f4df534bc184e372b02c4449b2|ctc_0df587760909a640016af9719bbd1887d18bc1d94de0edc1f9/1","name":"grep","args":"{\"pattern\":\"Tend|tend|saved goals\",\"path\":\"README.md\",\"limit\":25}","status":"ok","durationMs":9.653874999959953},{"id":"call_0435f3f4df534bc184e372b02c4449b2|ctc_0df587760909a640016af9719bbd1887d18bc1d94de0edc1f9/2","name":"read","args":"{\"path\":\"docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":35}","status":"ok","durationMs":0.7784159999573603},{"id":"call_0435f3f4df534bc184e372b02c4449b2|ctc_0df587760909a640016af9719bbd1887d18bc1d94de0edc1f9