PATH\"\n cargo +stable run --locked -- --home\n ```\n \n-Think is practice: no model calls or saved goals. Tend writes needs only when you\n-explicitly link or unlink. F2 (or Cmd+Enter, Ctrl+Alt+S; see [Function keys](docs/terminal-setup.md#function-keys)) sends, Enter adds a line, F1 lists what else you can do, Esc returns to the menu.\n+Think is practice: no model calls or saved goals. Tend saves thoughts only on `F2`\n+and writes needs only when you explicitly link or unlink. F2 (or Cmd+Enter, Ctrl+Alt+S; see [Function keys](docs/terminal-setup.md#function-keys)) sends, Enter adds a line, F1 lists what else you can do, Esc returns to the menu.\n Add `--snapshot` for text output.\n \n Real drafting needs a model and an explicitly authorized call allowance; provider\ndiff --git a/docs/design/architecture.md b/docs/design/architecture.md\nindex caae7ba..84ea5c2 100644\n--- a/docs/design/architecture.md\n+++ b/docs/design/architecture.md\n@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@ unconfirmed sessions or complete factory telemetry. The read-only\n | `measure/read.rs` | Bounded, cancellable `gh` reads scoped to the launch repo; no shell or retries. |\n | `measure/runs.rs`, `measure/runs/records.rs` | Closed-run postmortems: one explicit, cancellable read of tink-sdlc status, the run's labels, its steps' Pi launch logs and Git, then list and details. Unknown is never zero; no writes or providers. |\n | `tend/mod.rs` | The saved-goal garden's discovery states, selection and detail, with navigation to Shape and saved Think history. |\n+| `tend/thought.rs` | Repository-bound raw thoughts, explicit private atomic saving and the local read/editor view; no sessions, model sources or goal authority. |\n | `tend/connection.rs` | One bounded explicit request, latest exploration, source freshness and receipt coordination. |\n | `tend/connection/panel.rs` | Source and guidance review, explicit discovery, goal save and correction edits. |\n | `tend/connection/correction.rs` | One repository correction, bounded reads and stale-view-safe explicit replacement. |\n@@ -75,7 +76,7 @@ unconfirmed sessions or complete factory telemetry. The read-only\n | `worker.rs`, `worker/orientation.rs` | Bounded intake, stage and worker actions through SDLC, including whether a failed start permits retry or requires inspection. Recent Pi launch logs inform the operator’s cap choice. Only the explicitly configured allowance can reach the worker. |\n | `shape.rs` | Goals awaiting seeds; each session's confirmed goal, stage, folder, words, draft reading and next step. Reads and steps stay off the paint path. |\n | `shape/forms.rs` | Unsaved deferral and replacement-answer fields, navigation and cancellation; no validation or publication policy. |\n-| `shape/words.rs` | Shape's in-memory textarea adapter: editing, selection, cursor-following and original line-ending provenance; no save or agent policy. |\n+| `words.rs` | Shared exact-word textarea for Shape and Tend thoughts: editing, selection, cursor-following and original line-ending provenance; no save or agent policy. |\n | `shape/command.rs` | Shape without a screen: saving a goal's exact words, showing where a seed stands as JSON and taking one explicit step; it builds the same work the screen does and adds no ledger rule. |\n | `shape/step.rs`, `shape/prompt.txt` | The step's budget check, folder, model input, prompt, reply decoding and recording through the shared session boundary. Replies contain findings with a question or named seed prose fields; `seed_me` alone owns their layout and validation. |\n | `goal/mod.rs` | Goal parts, constraint normalisation and composing the goal block (shared). |\ndiff --git a/docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md b/docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\nindex b40011c..fb90d63 100644\n--- a/docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\n+++ b/docs/design/shape-and-handoff.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Tend and handoff\n \n-Tend holds saved goals; [Shape](#shape) asks its questions with an explicit\n+Tend holds saved goals and raw repository thoughts; [Shape](#shape) asks its questions with an explicit\n model and budget.\n \n ## Receipt\n@@ -25,6 +25,22 @@ claims readiness; other ended sessions are named as ended.\n \n ## Tend: garden and detail\n \n+In this repository's garden, `t` opens an exact-word thought editor. The screen names\n+the repository before `F2` saves. Esc cancels without saving. Saving makes no model\n+call and confirms no goal. Thoughts appear above the goal graph, labelled `Thought`.\n+`v` reads the saved thoughts; arrows select one and PgUp/PgDn scroll its words.\n+`g` copies the selected thought into a fresh, unsent Think visit. The existing\n+Think goal confirmation is still required. The thought stays unchanged on record.\n+Thoughts cannot open Shape and never enter Find connections in this slice.\n+\n+Thoughts use private atomic files under the captured Tend link root, separate from\n+sessions and goal confirmation records. Filenames bind the exact repository path\n+and exact UTF-8 words with SHA-256. Each record carries its repository explicitly.\n+Identical bytes in one repository keep one entry and report `Thought already saved`.\n+Whitespace and case differences remain distinct. Thoughts accept 1 to 131072 bytes;\n+empty or oversized input refuses without changing the editor. Existing records are\n+never edited or replaced. Read failures remain visible instead of becoming an empty list.\n+\n Inside a repository, Tend starts with only active goals whose verified creation\n origin names that exact repository root. A muted `this repo · a all` line offers\n `a` to show every active goal; `all · a this repo` toggles back. Outside a repo,\ndiff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs\nindex 08b0c63..8fedeac 100644\n--- a/src/lib.rs\n+++ b/src/lib.rs\n@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ pub mod think;\n pub mod think_record;\n pub mod voice;\n pub mod watch;\n+pub(crate) mod words;\n mod worker;\n \n /// Fit a single-line title into terminal cells, keeping whole graphemes and marking omitt